Where does the agent store its memory state?

00:07:07.516 --> 00:07:14.236
Agent needs memories and memory
option varies from short term to long term.

00:07:15.196 --> 00:07:19.356
The short term memory is the working memory of the agent.

00:07:20.716 --> 00:07:23.556
In the example of any company insurance agent,

00:07:23.596 --> 00:07:33.076
it can be something like the quote that is processing
currently the conversation history and the execution plan.

00:07:35.316 --> 00:07:44.476
And then it comes to the longer term stuff your semantic
memory via vector databases, the users profiles,

00:07:45.036 --> 00:07:52.316
and the episodic memory, which is the experience
and interaction the agent can recall.

00:07:53.236 --> 00:07:57.196
And often you will use tools to retrieve those memories.

00:07:58.596 --> 00:08:05.916
And last but not least, you also have prompts your system
prompts that is virtually controlled with your apps,

00:08:06.956 --> 00:08:10.516
and you can use that to tune the behavior of your agent.

00:08:11.716 --> 00:08:12.596
So in short.

00:08:15.076 --> 00:08:23.156
You have the short term memories that gets
the agents through one conversation,

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:29.276
