00:08:31.836 --> 00:08:40.596
Now, NCP modal context protocol is a standard way
for agents to communicate

00:08:40.876 --> 00:08:42.156
with your data stores.

00:08:43.556 --> 00:08:48.396
Think of it like a USB for your AI, right?

00:08:48.436 --> 00:08:54.876
It's a standard connector instead of one
custom connect for each data store.

00:08:56.156 --> 00:08:59.236
So if you look at the example on the screen,

00:08:59.236 --> 00:09:08.436
the agent doesn't have to know any implementation
detail of the data store because it can use the NCP servers.

00:09:08.916 --> 00:09:15.756
It is a standard connector and it's a clean
separation between the agent and the data store.

00:09:16.836 --> 00:09:23.316
As a result, you can actually swap out the data
store any time without changing the agent at all.

